WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.033 --> 00:02.233
This series was created for entertainment purposes.

3
00:02.234 --> 00:05.666
The characters, actions, locations, dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

4
00:05.667 --> 00:08.132
and artistic elements depicted in this series

5
00:08.133 --> 00:10.032
are fictional and based on imagination,

6
00:10.033 --> 00:13.933
incorporating the beauty of the region's diverse cultures,

7
00:13.934 --> 00:18.399
including those of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

8
00:18.400 --> 00:20.566
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

9
00:20.567 --> 00:23.601
ethnic group, organization, profession, or group of individuals.

10
00:23.602 --> 00:26.039
Viewer discretion is advised.

11
00:26.040 --> 00:28.440
[Previously] This is a grave matter, Mueang Fah.

12
00:28.441 --> 00:30.733
I believe you love Ullavee

13
00:30.734 --> 00:33.199
and you will not let someone like Prince Pha Wiang

14
00:33.200 --> 00:34.800
profit off our kingdom.

15
00:34.801 --> 00:37.433
What you've heard is false.

16
00:37.434 --> 00:38.800
But there were witnesses.

17
00:38.801 --> 00:39.900
Some people died.

18
00:39.901 --> 00:40.999
That wretched Mueang Fah.

19
00:41.000 --> 00:42.833
He keeps finding ways to cause me trouble at every turn.

20
00:42.834 --> 00:48.433
If you hadn't shown him a weakness to exploit, you wouldn't have to be angry now.

21
00:48.434 --> 00:50.066
That's the fortune-teller uncle.

22
00:50.067 --> 00:52.066
Fortune teller!

23
00:52.067 --> 00:53.334
Uncle!

24
01:00.501 --> 01:03.132
For patients with leg pain,

25
01:03.133 --> 01:05.767
the problem often originates in the piriformis muscle.

26
01:08.267 --> 01:10.999
Ma'am, may I?

27
01:11.000 --> 01:13.399
Ms. Boon, could you help me turn your mother over?

28
01:13.400 --> 01:15.266
- Yes. - Here we go.

29
01:15.267 --> 01:16.968
One, two, three.

30
01:18.167 --> 01:19.167
All right.

31
01:22.601 --> 01:24.934
The piriformis muscle is right here.

32
01:26.133 --> 01:27.968
This might hurt a little, ma'am.

33
01:31.968 --> 01:34.500
This is called piriformis syndrome.

34
01:34.501 --> 01:36.763
It happens when the piriformis muscle compresses a nerve.

35
01:36.764 --> 01:37.879
It usually occurs

36
01:37.880 --> 01:39.637
when someone stays in the same position for too long,

37
01:39.640 --> 01:41.840
whether sitting, standing, or lying down for extended periods,

38
01:41.840 --> 01:43.280
like your mother.

39
01:47.400 --> 01:52.199
This causes the piriformis muscle to tighten

40
01:52.200 --> 01:54.566
and put pressure on the sciatic nerve, resulting in leg pain.

41
01:54.567 --> 01:58.200
Some people may also experience numbness or muscle weakness.

42
02:00.267 --> 02:02.767
Let's have Na Boon help massage the muscle to loosen it up, ma'am.

43
02:06.334 --> 02:07.567
Right here.

44
02:11.334 --> 02:13.100
Form a triangle with your hands.

45
02:15.601 --> 02:17.166
May I?

46
02:17.167 --> 02:19.934
Link your thumbs together, then press down.

47
02:20.767 --> 02:22.701
Hold it for three seconds. That's right.

48
02:23.534 --> 02:26.133
It might sting a little, Mom, but you'll feel better.

49
02:36.667 --> 02:37.934
Good.

50
02:52.167 --> 02:54.167
Thank you so much, Mr. Bew.

51
02:56.767 --> 02:58.200
My pleasure.

52
03:04.680 --> 03:06.239
Don't forget to apply a warm compress to the painful area

53
03:06.240 --> 03:07.560
for your mom.

54
03:07.567 --> 03:10.399
10 to 20 minutes a day should be enough.

55
03:10.400 --> 03:12.800
My mom should sleep much better tonight.

56
03:12.801 --> 03:16.132
Thank you so much for teaching me the physical therapy exercises

57
03:16.133 --> 03:19.067
and even showing me those foot massage techniques.

58
03:20.133 --> 03:23.719
If you forget any of the exercises, just give me a call.

59
03:23.720 --> 03:25.999
And if you'd like to learn more about nutrition for your mom,

60
03:26.000 --> 03:27.600
let me know.

61
03:27.601 --> 03:29.666
I have a friend who can help.

62
03:29.667 --> 03:31.133
Thank you.

63
03:32.634 --> 03:35.766
Our next session is on Saturday, right?

64
03:35.767 --> 03:37.067
That's right.

65
03:49.100 --> 03:52.199
There's a glass door between us now, so I think it's okay.

66
03:52.200 --> 03:53.967
Could you take off your mask for a moment?

67
03:53.968 --> 03:57.300
In case we run into each other somewhere else, I'd like to be able to recognize you.

68
04:20.000 --> 04:21.701
Now we'll be able to recognize each other.

69
04:23.067 --> 04:25.133
Thank you for the drink.

70
04:26.968 --> 04:28.767
I hope you like it.

71
04:30.734 --> 04:32.200
Of course I do.

72
06:45.560 --> 06:50.280
[Star Dust]

73
07:29.868 --> 07:32.266
If I hadn't pulled you out of the way,

74
07:32.267 --> 07:34.334
that horse would've trampled you to death.

75
07:35.534 --> 07:39.133
Every time we cross paths, you're always one step from dying.

76
07:40.400 --> 07:43.079
I was just out for a walk.

77
07:43.080 --> 07:44.080
Look who's talking.

78
07:44.081 --> 07:47.880
Every time you show up, I nearly get myself killed.

79
07:49.934 --> 07:51.933
So now it's my fault?

80
07:51.934 --> 07:54.501
I never said it was anyone's fault.

81
07:57.133 --> 07:58.334
Never mind.

82
07:59.434 --> 08:01.067
Anyway...

83
08:03.100 --> 08:06.567
Thank you for saving my life.

84
08:07.167 --> 08:11.399
And thank you...

85
08:11.400 --> 08:13.834
for giving me a reason to live again.

86
08:19.834 --> 08:21.601
I've been thinking...

87
08:23.234 --> 08:25.400
about what you said the other day.

88
08:26.634 --> 08:29.199
You were right.

89
08:29.200 --> 08:34.167
We're not born... just to die.

90
08:35.534 --> 08:37.666
So I've made up my mind.

91
08:37.667 --> 08:40.233
I'm going to make the most of my life.

92
08:40.234 --> 08:42.200
I'm going to have a blast!

93
09:03.467 --> 09:04.968
Hey! Wait!

94
09:16.033 --> 09:18.333
If we meet again,

95
09:18.334 --> 09:20.700
I hope you're still alive.

96
09:20.701 --> 09:23.233
Why would you say that, Your Highness?

97
09:23.234 --> 09:25.200
Of course I'll still be alive!

98
09:25.934 --> 09:28.266
I'm going to live a long, happy life.

99
09:28.267 --> 09:30.867
After all, I've been given a second chance as a noblewoman.

100
09:30.868 --> 09:34.267
I'm going to live like a fabulous lady!

101
09:38.801 --> 09:40.868
You're as ridiculous as ever.

102
09:42.560 --> 09:43.280
I'll see you

103
09:43.280 --> 09:45.440
at Prince Kong Tai's birthday celebration, Your Highness.

104
09:47.968 --> 09:49.534
You'll be there, won't you?

105
10:07.868 --> 10:09.234
Where am I now?

106
10:10.334 --> 10:11.567
How do I get back?

107
10:15.267 --> 10:16.300
But...

108
10:17.667 --> 10:19.733
I came from that way.

109
10:19.734 --> 10:22.400
So... I should just go back that way.

110
10:33.033 --> 10:34.801
You've been through a lot.

111
10:37.634 --> 10:41.566
You lost your parents and the people you loved.

112
10:41.567 --> 10:44.767
Your boyfriend sucks. Your friend betrayed you.

113
10:45.467 --> 10:46.567
Am I right?

114
10:48.467 --> 10:49.667
Eva.

115
10:51.200 --> 10:52.467
The fortune teller.

116
11:01.467 --> 11:03.234
Lady Fongnuan.

117
11:04.434 --> 11:06.534
Why are you still awake?

118
11:09.467 --> 11:13.601
If you stay out in the night air for too long, you'll fall ill.

119
11:14.267 --> 11:15.934
I can't stop thinking about it.

120
11:18.100 --> 11:19.534
Eva...

121
11:22.467 --> 11:24.433
Lha...

122
11:24.434 --> 11:28.800
You said... we have 32 souls.

123
11:28.801 --> 11:31.200
Almost as if we have 32 lives.

124
11:35.667 --> 11:37.701
Does that mean...

125
11:39.033 --> 11:42.800
When we die, can we be reborn?

126
11:42.801 --> 11:46.033
Can we meet again in another life?

127
11:46.634 --> 11:49.334
Is that what's keeping you awake?

128
11:51.834 --> 11:54.700
As long as our souls stay with us,

129
11:54.701 --> 11:57.399
we remain healthy and well.

130
11:57.400 --> 12:01.500
But when they leave, we fall ill.

131
12:01.501 --> 12:07.400
We have to perform a ritual... to call them back.

132
12:09.167 --> 12:13.766
If they don't return, we die.

133
12:13.767 --> 12:19.099
Then our 32 souls are reborn into 32 new lives.

134
12:19.100 --> 12:24.266
Perhaps we've died and been reborn many times.

135
12:24.267 --> 12:27.033
Only to meet in this life, my lady.

136
12:42.267 --> 12:44.267
So, besides me...

137
12:46.467 --> 12:48.033
Eva...

138
12:49.033 --> 12:50.834
and the fortune teller,

139
12:53.400 --> 12:55.567
who else will show up?

140
13:19.467 --> 13:21.267
Welcome, Your Highness.

141
13:28.000 --> 13:29.567
Prince Mueang Fah.

142
13:32.167 --> 13:33.801
You're here too?

143
13:35.434 --> 13:36.734
Mueang Fah!

144
13:38.601 --> 13:40.766
You two know each other?

145
13:40.767 --> 13:42.766
When did you meet?

146
13:42.767 --> 13:45.466
How did you meet?

147
13:45.467 --> 13:48.800
That's a long story. Want to hear it?

148
13:48.801 --> 13:50.234
Don't you dare.

149
13:53.334 --> 13:55.199
Today is Kong Tai's birthday.

150
13:55.200 --> 13:56.999
Let's not keep the celebrations waiting.

151
13:57.000 --> 14:00.400
Let's raise our cups and wish Kong Tai a happy birthday.

152
14:03.267 --> 14:04.733
But...

153
14:04.734 --> 14:07.868
The seer told me to keep the Five Precepts.

154
14:14.434 --> 14:16.733
But it's my birthday.

155
14:16.734 --> 14:19.434
Surely one little drink won't hurt.

156
14:21.400 --> 14:25.701
Then let's drink to our hearts' content. And no one leaves early.

157
14:29.801 --> 14:33.234
Have a wonderful time. I've taken care of everything.

158
14:57.067 --> 15:01.800
This celebration is my birthday gift to you.

159
15:01.801 --> 15:06.533
Everyone here joins me in raising a toast to you, Kong Tai.

160
15:06.534 --> 15:09.834
I'm afraid I haven't brought you a gift.

161
15:11.167 --> 15:13.767
You'll have to accept Saen Thep's gift on my behalf.

162
15:15.834 --> 15:17.367
Thank you, Sister.

163
15:32.501 --> 15:34.233
And this...

164
15:34.234 --> 15:35.868
is my gift to you.

165
15:51.033 --> 15:53.133
What a beautiful dagger!

166
15:54.000 --> 15:55.667
I love it!

167
15:59.033 --> 16:01.533
Kong Tai. Careful!

168
16:01.534 --> 16:02.868
Watch this.

169
16:05.033 --> 16:06.534
Kong Tai!

170
16:07.167 --> 16:08.634
Put that away.

171
16:13.534 --> 16:17.000
And here's... my gift to you.

172
16:20.033 --> 16:21.033
Fongnuan.

173
16:26.467 --> 16:31.466
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

174
16:31.467 --> 16:36.132
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

175
16:36.133 --> 16:37.199
♪ Happy birth- ♪

176
16:37.200 --> 16:38.968
What on earth are you singing?

177
16:39.734 --> 16:41.534
I haven't the faintest idea what that means.

178
16:48.968 --> 16:51.167
I haven't even finished the song!

179
16:52.334 --> 16:54.501
How can you judge it already?

180
17:04.434 --> 17:08.633
Was that a birthday song...

181
17:08.634 --> 17:10.667
from Wang Nam Lin?

182
17:17.834 --> 17:19.567
Yes, Your Highness.

183
17:21.167 --> 17:23.166
Everyone in Wang Nam Lin...

184
17:23.167 --> 17:25.400
knows that song.

185
17:28.601 --> 17:29.801
I see.

186
17:32.968 --> 17:37.399
That song is going to be a huge hit. Everyone around the world will sing it.

187
17:37.400 --> 17:39.634
Let's hear the rest of it!

188
17:40.734 --> 17:45.500
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

189
17:45.501 --> 17:50.132
- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪ - Yoo. Yoo!

190
17:50.133 --> 17:55.199
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪

191
17:55.200 --> 18:00.601
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

192
18:03.434 --> 18:08.100
Why doesn't everyone sing along? The more, the merrier.

193
18:11.133 --> 18:15.066
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

194
18:15.067 --> 18:20.701
- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪ - Yoo... Heavens!

195
18:22.267 --> 18:24.633
You all carry on.

196
18:24.634 --> 18:26.300
My head hurts!

197
18:30.734 --> 18:32.501
My ears hurt.

198
18:50.601 --> 18:53.733
It was only the slow version.

199
18:53.734 --> 18:56.466
Now, let's try the more upbeat version.

200
18:56.467 --> 18:58.566
Dance! Prince Fah Haam.

201
18:58.567 --> 19:01.400
Dans? Dans?

202
19:08.520 --> 19:09.839
All right!

203
19:09.840 --> 19:11.633
Kong Tai,

204
19:11.634 --> 19:17.567
I offer this performance to you... as a birthday gift.

205
19:23.267 --> 19:27.132
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

206
19:27.133 --> 19:30.399
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪ Come on!

207
19:30.400 --> 19:35.901
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪

208
19:36.968 --> 19:38.767
♪ Happy birth... ♪

209
19:39.601 --> 19:42.200
♪ Happy birth... ♪

210
19:45.133 --> 19:46.666
♪ Day ♪

211
19:46.667 --> 19:47.999
Just say it.

212
19:48.000 --> 19:49.967
♪ To you ♪

213
19:49.968 --> 19:51.766
- ♪ Yooo... ♪ - ♪ Yooo... ♪

214
19:51.767 --> 19:52.901
Yoo!

215
19:54.400 --> 19:55.834
Yoo.

216
19:56.634 --> 19:58.600
Prince Kong Tai.

217
19:58.601 --> 20:00.200
♪ Happy birth... ♪

218
20:01.200 --> 20:02.566
Just follow my lead.

219
20:02.567 --> 20:05.399
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪ Come on!

220
20:05.400 --> 20:10.800
- ♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪ - Day!

221
20:10.801 --> 20:14.433
♪ Happy birthday to... ♪

222
20:14.434 --> 20:16.801
- You! - Yoo!

223
20:18.367 --> 20:20.967
- You! - Yoo!

224
20:20.968 --> 20:22.366
That's right.

225
20:22.367 --> 20:25.066
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

226
20:25.067 --> 20:26.166
- You! - Yoo!

227
20:26.167 --> 20:28.299
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

228
20:28.300 --> 20:30.066
- You! - Yoo!

229
20:30.067 --> 20:34.099
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

230
20:34.100 --> 20:37.166
♪ Happy birthday to... ♪

231
20:37.167 --> 20:39.601
- You! - Yoo!

232
20:47.567 --> 20:49.333
♪ Happy birthday to... ♪

233
20:49.334 --> 20:52.634
- You! - Yoo!

234
20:53.367 --> 20:56.167
What on earth are you all singing?

235
20:57.133 --> 20:58.434
Indraraja.

236
21:03.767 --> 21:05.634
There's no need to stand on ceremony.

237
21:09.133 --> 21:12.200
I'm here to give you my blessings as your elder brother.

238
21:14.567 --> 21:15.667
Have a seat.

239
21:35.367 --> 21:36.467
Hey.

240
21:55.801 --> 21:57.200
Is that...

241
21:57.868 --> 22:02.566
the jade chest the Chin Haw merchant gave Father?

242
22:02.567 --> 22:03.734
It is.

243
22:05.234 --> 22:06.834
It's yours now.

244
22:07.767 --> 22:09.067
Take it.

245
22:10.834 --> 22:11.901
I...

246
22:14.234 --> 22:17.133
- I can't accept it. - Why not?

247
22:17.734 --> 22:19.501
Because I want you to have it!

248
22:26.133 --> 22:28.100
What a drunken fool.

249
22:30.801 --> 22:32.867
But I don't want it.

250
22:32.868 --> 22:35.166
It belongs to Father.

251
22:35.167 --> 22:36.433
You should keep it.

252
22:36.434 --> 22:39.032
How dare you disobey me, Kong Tai?

253
22:39.033 --> 22:41.367
I'm sure Kong Tai didn't mean to offend you.

254
22:47.234 --> 22:50.834
Perhaps he thinks your gift is simply too precious to accept.

255
22:53.133 --> 22:54.600
You...

256
22:54.601 --> 22:59.834
Once I'm on the throne, everything in this palace will be mine.

257
23:00.400 --> 23:02.601
I can give whatever I want to whoever I please.

258
23:04.601 --> 23:06.334
Isn't that right?

259
23:31.067 --> 23:33.132
The Crown Prince...

260
23:33.133 --> 23:36.234
is simply trying to show his generosity toward Kong Tai.

261
23:38.200 --> 23:41.067
He may have been a little forceful in making his offer,

262
23:41.734 --> 23:43.667
but I'm sure you understand.

263
23:46.968 --> 23:52.434
Indraraja has brought this jade chest, a treasured possession of Father.

264
23:53.567 --> 23:55.467
Since he brought it to give you his blessing.

265
23:56.033 --> 24:01.400
Let's accept it as a blessing from Father himself.

266
24:03.667 --> 24:06.033
As for a personal gift from Indraraja himself,

267
24:07.400 --> 24:09.267
he'll arrange something else for you later.

268
24:10.033 --> 24:11.534
Would that satisfy you?

269
24:20.868 --> 24:22.200
Very well.

270
24:28.434 --> 24:30.233
I'll take my leave, then.

271
24:30.234 --> 24:33.067
Allow me to escort you back to your residence.

272
25:31.834 --> 25:34.634
Bottoms up!

273
25:42.067 --> 25:44.933
Hey! You're the birthday boy!

274
25:44.934 --> 25:47.399
You can't be the first one to pass out!

275
25:47.400 --> 25:50.601
I can't keep up with you two!

276
25:54.234 --> 25:56.267
I have to concede defeat to you too, junior.

277
25:57.434 --> 26:00.933
You're quite the drinker.

278
26:00.934 --> 26:03.800
Then let's have another round. Come on.

279
26:03.801 --> 26:05.666
Lady Fongnuan.

280
26:05.667 --> 26:07.234
Senior.

281
26:08.133 --> 26:10.333
Lha.

282
26:10.334 --> 26:12.000
No, my lady.

283
26:13.133 --> 26:15.366
You really don't know a good thing when you see it.

284
26:15.367 --> 26:17.234
Prince Kong Tai, keep going.

285
26:18.968 --> 26:20.399
Cheers!

286
26:20.400 --> 26:22.067
- Shia! - Shia!

287
26:28.033 --> 26:30.333
Let's return to your residence, my lady.

288
26:30.334 --> 26:31.967
We can't leave yet, Lha.

289
26:31.968 --> 26:35.766
There's still plenty of liquor left.

290
26:35.767 --> 26:39.867
And this is homemade sato.

291
26:39.868 --> 26:43.067
I've never had sato this good.

292
26:43.667 --> 26:46.566
It'd be a shame to leave it unfinished.

293
26:46.567 --> 26:50.667
But Princess Maneethip and Prince Saen Thep left ages ago.

294
26:51.834 --> 26:54.266
We shouldn't keep them waiting or worrying.

295
26:54.267 --> 26:56.666
Come on, Lha.

296
26:56.667 --> 26:59.833
Why do you have to bring up those revered names?

297
26:59.834 --> 27:01.600
Fine. I'll stop drinking.

298
27:01.601 --> 27:03.266
I'm leaving now.

299
27:03.267 --> 27:07.233
Very well. I'll return to my residence.

300
27:07.234 --> 27:09.366
Enjoy yourselves, Your Highnesses.

301
27:09.367 --> 27:12.834
But next time, we're going to...

302
27:13.534 --> 27:15.901
drink till sunrise!

303
27:16.567 --> 27:19.400
Good night, Your Highness. Good night. Good night.

304
27:20.334 --> 27:21.868
Good heavens, Lady Fongnuan!

305
27:23.934 --> 27:25.766
Good night! Good night!

306
27:25.767 --> 27:27.233
- Drink till sunrise. - Lady Fongnuan.

307
27:27.234 --> 27:29.800
You're speaking that strange language again.

308
27:29.801 --> 27:31.266
Drink till sunrise?

309
27:31.267 --> 27:33.567
- Gud nai? - What does that mean?

310
27:34.467 --> 27:35.868
Junior!

311
27:39.934 --> 27:43.267
We can... ask her again tomorrow.

312
27:49.334 --> 27:50.501
Here.

313
27:52.434 --> 27:54.666
- Shia! - Shia!

314
27:54.667 --> 27:56.000
Shia.

315
28:00.334 --> 28:02.032
Good heavens!

316
28:02.033 --> 28:04.032
What's wrong, Kong Tai?

317
28:04.033 --> 28:08.467
The seer warned me not to leave my residence after dark.

318
28:10.868 --> 28:12.601
And it's already late.

319
28:13.467 --> 28:14.767
I must go.

320
28:18.567 --> 28:20.067
Kong Tai.

321
28:34.801 --> 28:36.067
Shia!

322
28:42.968 --> 28:44.133
Shia.

323
29:03.567 --> 29:10.366
♪ Happi birdday to yoo! ♪

324
29:10.367 --> 29:12.466
♪ Yoo! ♪

325
29:12.467 --> 29:16.667
♪ Birdday... yoo! ♪

326
29:21.200 --> 29:22.600
Move!

327
29:22.601 --> 29:24.399
Get out of the way!

328
29:24.400 --> 29:25.834
Move!

329
29:26.968 --> 29:28.200
Move!

330
29:36.000 --> 29:37.433
A woman.

331
29:37.434 --> 29:38.901
Pretty.

332
29:40.801 --> 29:42.234
Hey!

333
29:45.868 --> 29:47.501
No!

334
29:54.534 --> 29:56.267
Do you have a death wish?

335
29:59.834 --> 30:01.666
I was just singing.

336
30:01.667 --> 30:05.199
If you don't want to get hurt, keep your shrill voice down.

337
30:05.200 --> 30:06.801
You startled my horse.

338
30:11.734 --> 30:15.433
So, what's your name?

339
30:15.434 --> 30:18.266
I could sing for you instead.

340
30:18.267 --> 30:19.366
Just look at you.

341
30:19.367 --> 30:21.767
I doubt you could even find your way back to your residence.

342
30:22.567 --> 30:24.601
Hey! Wait!

343
30:44.968 --> 30:49.868
♪ Happi birdday to yoo! ♪

344
31:06.567 --> 31:08.133
You should leave now.

345
31:23.734 --> 31:27.000
I've only just woken up, and you're already trying to get rid of me.

346
31:37.767 --> 31:39.800
What's wrong?

347
31:39.801 --> 31:42.133
Why the long face?

348
31:49.300 --> 31:51.500
Your clothes...

349
31:51.501 --> 31:54.901
were made with exquisite skill by master weavers.

350
31:57.400 --> 32:01.366
Your ornament is made of pure silver and bears the royal emblem of the steed.

351
32:01.367 --> 32:05.233
It identifies you as one of the King's six sons.

352
32:05.234 --> 32:07.333
A commoner like you

353
32:07.334 --> 32:11.467
could never have obtained such an ornament, let alone stolen it.

354
32:12.634 --> 32:15.434
- You've been lying all this time. - I never lied to you.

355
32:18.934 --> 32:20.968
I merely kept the truth from you.

356
32:24.767 --> 32:27.067
I had to hide who I was,

357
32:28.534 --> 32:30.801
but my love for you...

358
32:32.267 --> 32:33.801
is real.

359
32:35.033 --> 32:36.968
Every bit of it.

360
32:40.100 --> 32:42.534
You have two choices.

361
32:43.200 --> 32:46.967
First, never come here again.

362
32:46.968 --> 32:50.166
Second, you may keep coming here,

363
32:50.167 --> 32:51.733
but you must never see me again.

364
32:51.734 --> 32:53.267
I choose neither.

365
32:53.868 --> 32:58.132
I told you I wanted nothing to do with people of high station.

366
32:58.133 --> 33:00.600
I dislike life in Wiang Kaew.

367
33:00.601 --> 33:02.967
If you ever try to buy my freedom,

368
33:02.968 --> 33:04.901
you'll never see me again.

369
33:10.901 --> 33:13.501
You cast me aside without a second thought.

370
33:15.234 --> 33:17.299
Do you not love me at all?

371
33:17.300 --> 33:19.300
All this time, I never knew.

372
33:19.968 --> 33:22.266
But now I do.

373
33:22.267 --> 33:24.667
I cannot accept it.

374
33:28.300 --> 33:31.567
Your world terrifies me. I want no part of it.

375
33:36.434 --> 33:38.567
I want to live.

376
33:39.534 --> 33:41.501
Please, leave me be.

377
33:42.334 --> 33:43.934
We must never meet again.

378
34:42.234 --> 34:44.167
What happened here?

379
35:00.167 --> 35:02.100
Who did this?

380
35:10.000 --> 35:11.334
Who did this?

381
35:15.133 --> 35:17.333
I did.

382
35:17.334 --> 35:20.299
I know you made these hawk's-eye amulets,

383
35:20.300 --> 35:22.633
but who destroyed them?

384
35:22.634 --> 35:24.366
Exactly.

385
35:24.367 --> 35:28.633
I'd like to know who could be so cruel, too.

386
35:28.634 --> 35:32.233
I spent days and nights making them.

387
35:32.234 --> 35:36.666
Lha even brought over a huge bundle of bamboo. Then we carved them until our hands were raw.

388
35:36.667 --> 35:38.400
And now they're all ruined.

389
35:41.801 --> 35:44.366
Are you really so upset?

390
35:44.367 --> 35:46.067
Of course I am.

391
35:47.067 --> 35:49.032
They were meant to...

392
35:49.033 --> 35:53.166
bring blessings, ward off evil spirits,

393
35:53.167 --> 35:56.100
and protect Prince Kong Tai from further misfortune.

394
35:57.868 --> 35:59.701
But look at them.

395
36:00.400 --> 36:04.067
They're all ruined. They can't protect anyone now.

396
36:06.667 --> 36:09.366
You seem to care a great deal about Kong Tai.

397
36:09.367 --> 36:13.166
You made him gifts, sang for him,

398
36:13.167 --> 36:15.434
and now you're even collecting his gifts for him.

399
36:18.667 --> 36:20.667
You came here to retrieve something, too.

400
36:25.334 --> 36:27.600
If Prince Indraraja finds out,

401
36:27.601 --> 36:29.766
will there be another scene?

402
36:29.767 --> 36:33.267
As long as you keep quiet, no one will find out.

403
36:34.033 --> 36:36.033
I'll take care of the rest.

404
36:39.100 --> 36:40.667
Prince Mueang Fah.

405
36:43.734 --> 36:46.133
You may seem rather stern,

406
36:46.701 --> 36:49.934
but you do care about your siblings.

407
37:02.234 --> 37:05.701
Yes, Your Highness. I'll say no more.

408
37:29.634 --> 37:31.934
Lha!

409
37:35.234 --> 37:39.067
Indraraja must have promised to take him back to Ullavee.

410
37:39.767 --> 37:41.801
That's why he's taken Indraraja's side.

411
37:42.367 --> 37:47.266
Then why not ask Father to lift the order of exile,

412
37:47.267 --> 37:50.100
and let Mueang Fah stay here with us?

413
37:50.801 --> 37:55.367
Then he would have no reason to side with Indraraja.

414
37:58.267 --> 37:59.367
No.

415
38:01.300 --> 38:03.766
I don't want him anywhere near me.

416
38:03.767 --> 38:08.934
Ever since your brother arrived in Ullavee, your father hasn't once asked to see me.

417
38:11.100 --> 38:12.800
He's a bringer of misfortune.

418
38:12.801 --> 38:17.166
Mother. I doubt he has anything to do with that.

419
38:17.167 --> 38:20.800
Don't talk back to me. Go earn some glory on the battlefield.

420
38:20.801 --> 38:23.733
The realm is at peace.

421
38:23.734 --> 38:25.667
Who am I supposed to fight?

422
38:27.200 --> 38:28.933
Then hurry up and marry.

423
38:28.934 --> 38:31.133
Find a consort of higher standing than Saen Thep's.

424
38:34.400 --> 38:36.400
What does that have to do with anything?

425
38:38.267 --> 38:41.066
Through Saen Thep's marriage to Maneethip,

426
38:41.067 --> 38:44.000
your father has secured a great deal of salt from Wang Nam Lin.

427
38:45.133 --> 38:47.133
Salt is scarce.

428
38:47.901 --> 38:52.166
Wang Nam Lin is a small city with barely any troops.

429
38:52.167 --> 38:54.901
Its wealth comes entirely from its salt fields.

430
38:59.033 --> 39:01.666
You must find a consort

431
39:01.667 --> 39:03.968
who brings more than Saen Thep's does.

432
39:56.834 --> 39:59.800
Lady Fongnuan, don't you remember?

433
39:59.801 --> 40:02.533
Lha, just tell me.

434
40:02.534 --> 40:07.033
Then we can make her happy.

435
40:12.234 --> 40:14.800
Before she met Prince Saen Thep,

436
40:14.801 --> 40:17.734
Princess Maneethip was already in love with someone else.

437
40:21.934 --> 40:24.000
General In Saeng.

438
40:27.701 --> 40:30.600
They had grown up together.

439
40:30.601 --> 40:34.533
General In Saeng was a loyal man.

440
40:34.534 --> 40:38.868
He had always protected and looked after Princess Maneethip.

441
40:39.667 --> 40:43.467
He was also the one who taught her to ride.

442
40:48.200 --> 40:53.033
Over time, their closeness grew into love.

443
40:56.734 --> 41:00.900
But before they could confess their feelings,

444
41:00.901 --> 41:04.868
Prince Saen Thep met Princess Maneethip.

445
41:29.000 --> 41:33.333
His Highness asked King Chai Saen Lue

446
41:33.334 --> 41:36.868
to send a royal proposal for Princess Maneethip's hand in marriage.

447
41:38.634 --> 41:40.967
Your uncle agreed to the match.

448
41:40.968 --> 41:46.234
He approved Princess Maneethip's marriage to Prince Saen Thep.

449
41:47.100 --> 41:51.701
And he sent General In Saeng to serve at the city border.

450
42:14.033 --> 42:16.834
And we were sent here.

451
42:17.734 --> 42:19.900
From that day on,

452
42:19.901 --> 42:24.666
Princess Maneethip and General In Saeng

453
42:24.667 --> 42:26.801
never saw each other again.

454
42:30.033 --> 42:35.534
Wang Nam Lin is a small city with no army to speak of.

455
42:36.467 --> 42:40.934
We must depend on Ullavee, a far greater kingdom.

456
42:43.968 --> 42:48.367
Prince Saen Thep is third in line to the throne.

457
42:50.200 --> 42:56.433
Your uncle needs Ullavee's military strength

458
42:56.434 --> 43:00.434
to keep the bandits and rebels at bay.

459
43:09.367 --> 43:15.400
It was a marriage of convenience,

460
43:16.467 --> 43:18.367
not love.

461
43:22.000 --> 43:24.767
Even after hundreds of years,

462
43:26.567 --> 43:28.267
such arrangements...

463
43:29.367 --> 43:31.067
still exist.

464
43:35.000 --> 43:36.901
Is it possible...

465
43:38.400 --> 43:41.200
to marry someone for love,

466
43:44.334 --> 43:46.934
out of genuine affection,

467
43:48.033 --> 43:51.166
with nothing to gain from it?

468
43:51.167 --> 43:53.234
That would be difficult, my lady.

469
43:54.100 --> 43:57.366
Princes and princesses

470
43:57.367 --> 44:00.601
must always marry out of duty.

471
44:04.901 --> 44:09.534
But Prince Saen Thep treats Princess Maneethip very well.

472
44:10.767 --> 44:13.367
He does everything he can to pamper her.

473
44:15.200 --> 44:19.200
Yet Princess Maneethip still refuses to open her heart to him.

474
44:23.601 --> 44:26.100
My heart aches for them both.

475
44:29.834 --> 44:34.801
I hope she and Prince Saen Thep...

476
44:38.701 --> 44:40.667
can get through this.

477
44:44.200 --> 44:45.801
At least...

478
44:46.534 --> 44:49.434
their wedding night...

479
44:53.434 --> 44:56.701
should be a happy occasion for them both.

480
45:42.634 --> 45:45.467
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Sukantha. - I bow before you, Royal Consort Sukantha.

481
45:47.200 --> 45:50.133
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or. - I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

482
45:53.100 --> 45:58.066
We are deeply honored by your presence, Royal Consort Sukantha.

483
45:58.067 --> 46:02.567
As the inner court's representative, it is my duty to attend.

484
46:08.400 --> 46:10.434
What a modest ceremony.

485
46:11.067 --> 46:15.734
Quite fitting for a consort from a small city like Wang Nam Lin.

486
47:01.567 --> 47:05.100
What does the full bedding ceremony involve?

487
47:06.200 --> 47:10.199
After the Soul-Blessing Ceremony, which wards off misfortune

488
47:10.200 --> 47:13.666
and blesses the bride and groom with a lifetime of love.

489
47:13.667 --> 47:17.066
Their family members tie blessed cotton threads around their wrists.

490
47:17.067 --> 47:19.434
And offer them their blessings.

491
47:20.033 --> 47:22.000
Then the couple is escorted to the bridal chamber.

492
47:28.667 --> 47:30.132
There.

493
47:30.133 --> 47:32.133
The master of ceremonies is here.

494
47:36.701 --> 47:38.234
The fortune teller?

495
47:51.434 --> 47:52.968
What fortune teller?

496
47:54.934 --> 47:56.433
That uncle.

497
47:56.434 --> 47:57.868
Who is he, Your Highness?

498
47:58.934 --> 48:00.500
Seer Phrommaya.

499
48:00.501 --> 48:05.500
Royal Consort Chiang La-or invited him to conduct the blessing ceremony.

500
48:05.501 --> 48:06.734
A seer?

501
48:07.767 --> 48:09.434
A royal seer?

502
48:10.801 --> 48:12.667
What in the world?

503
48:24.667 --> 48:26.399
Goodness!

504
48:26.400 --> 48:27.833
What took you so long?

505
48:27.834 --> 48:30.200
I thought you'd show up at the end to help clean up.

506
48:31.934 --> 48:34.867
I went to fetch Fah Haam first.

507
48:34.868 --> 48:37.099
I had to drag him out of bed.

508
48:37.100 --> 48:38.701
Now I'm starving.

509
48:39.801 --> 48:41.968
Is food all you ever think about?

510
48:45.133 --> 48:48.266
What happened to you?

511
48:48.267 --> 48:52.533
Goodness! Did you fall into a wine barrel, Your Highness?

512
48:52.534 --> 48:55.733
Just look at you. You look like a man with a broken heart.

513
48:55.734 --> 48:58.566
Do they have any sato? Can I have a drink now?

514
48:58.567 --> 49:02.266
Please? Will you stop asking for a drink?

515
49:02.267 --> 49:05.133
Have some mercy. I have to observe the Five Precepts.

516
49:22.634 --> 49:24.167
Mueang Fah.

517
49:32.067 --> 49:33.334
Bew!

518
49:41.934 --> 49:43.100
Babe.

519
49:46.234 --> 49:48.534
Here, here. Hey!

520
49:51.400 --> 49:55.300
- That hurts. - I'm sorry.

521
50:07.133 --> 50:08.400
Bew?

522
50:21.634 --> 50:27.399
After Indraraja, Mueang Fah, and Prince Pha Wiang arrived.

523
50:27.400 --> 50:29.733
Why do you look like you've seen a ghost?

524
50:29.734 --> 50:31.999
A ghost would've been better.

525
50:32.000 --> 50:34.400
I never want to see him again in this lifetime.

526
50:35.968 --> 50:38.132
Wait, what's the name of the man

527
50:38.133 --> 50:42.800
who just arrived with Prince Indraraja and Prince Mueang Fah?

528
50:42.801 --> 50:44.467
Prince Pha Wiang.

529
50:47.467 --> 50:49.833
The Crown Prince of Merng Mang.

530
50:49.834 --> 50:52.200
He's Indraraja's cousin.

531
50:53.634 --> 50:57.600
Prince Pha Wiang's father was the elder brother of Indraraja's mother,

532
50:57.601 --> 51:00.033
the late Queen Chao Oun.

533
51:00.834 --> 51:02.000
Junior.

534
51:03.067 --> 51:04.501
Do you know him?

535
51:11.267 --> 51:13.133
No, Your Highness.

536
51:14.968 --> 51:17.132
I don't. That's why I asked.

537
51:17.133 --> 51:22.200
I don't want to put my foot in my mouth and end up losing my head.

538
51:23.801 --> 51:25.600
Well, then...

539
51:25.601 --> 51:27.867
I'll take my leave.

540
51:27.868 --> 51:30.501
I'd rather go see Maneethip.

541
51:46.234 --> 51:47.734
Fah Haam.

542
51:50.400 --> 51:52.167
Don't handle me so roughly,

543
51:52.767 --> 51:54.133
or I might throw up.

544
51:55.067 --> 51:58.467
I was only going to ask you to move over. I need to sit down.

545
52:09.667 --> 52:11.601
This might make you feel better.

546
52:21.334 --> 52:23.701
That's Prince Pha Wiang, Boon.

547
52:24.901 --> 52:26.534
He's not Bew.

548
52:30.567 --> 52:32.333
That woman.

549
52:32.334 --> 52:34.266
Who is she?

550
52:34.267 --> 52:37.266
Lady Fongnuan, a younger cousin of Princess Maneethip,

551
52:37.267 --> 52:39.533
Prince Saen Thep's consort.

552
52:39.534 --> 52:41.366
I see.

553
52:41.367 --> 52:42.968
So she's no stranger to the court.

554
52:44.834 --> 52:47.099
But she seems a little unhinged.

555
52:47.100 --> 52:48.667
Quite mad.

556
53:07.133 --> 53:09.067
Your bride has arrived.

557
53:46.200 --> 53:47.901
I know you're exhausted,

558
53:49.000 --> 53:52.167
but remember to keep smiling throughout today's ceremony.

559
54:39.934 --> 54:41.934
Please take good care of my cousin, Your Highness.

560
55:13.934 --> 55:17.834
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty. - I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

561
55:18.534 --> 55:20.400
King Chai Saen Lue.

562
56:20.467 --> 56:22.333
These blessed cotton threads...

563
56:22.334 --> 56:26.566
will bind your wrists for this night alone,

564
56:26.567 --> 56:30.999
but may love bind...

565
56:31.000 --> 56:33.968
your hearts for all eternity.

566
56:34.901 --> 56:38.000
May you love and cherish each other,

567
56:38.734 --> 56:41.968
and be blessed with many children and grandchildren.

568
57:39.467 --> 57:45.934
According to records from neighboring cities, Ullavee's last king was a cruel man.

569
57:46.501 --> 57:50.334
He killed his own siblings to seize the throne.

570
57:54.634 --> 57:58.566
Most of the princes had different mothers,

571
57:58.567 --> 58:01.433
yet they'd been close since childhood.

572
58:01.434 --> 58:04.633
Alas, no matter how much they loved one another,

573
58:04.634 --> 58:09.701
when the time came to fight for power, the struggle was brutal.

574
58:56.467 --> 58:59.067
Today is the happiest day of my life.

575
58:59.968 --> 59:02.434
I'm so glad you're my consort.

576
59:05.801 --> 59:10.868
I promise to love and care for you.

577
59:13.367 --> 59:15.734
I'll never cause you sorrow.

578
59:43.667 --> 59:45.701
So this is your answer.

579
59:52.334 --> 59:53.968
All this time,

580
59:56.167 --> 59:58.467
you never wished to marry me,

581
01:00:02.434 --> 01:00:05.200
nor did you ever love me, did you?

582
01:00:15.467 --> 01:00:17.367
My feelings...

583
01:00:19.200 --> 01:00:20.801
are of no consequence.

584
01:00:28.434 --> 01:00:31.234
Duty must come before the heart, Your Highness.

585
01:01:10.601 --> 01:01:12.701
My cousin is married now.

586
01:01:13.367 --> 01:01:15.601
It's just the two of us left.

587
01:01:16.667 --> 01:01:18.666
It feels a little lonely, doesn't it?

588
01:01:18.667 --> 01:01:20.000
Yes, my lady.

589
01:01:34.267 --> 01:01:35.567
Lha.

590
01:01:38.534 --> 01:01:40.367
On the wedding night,

591
01:01:41.968 --> 01:01:44.501
isn't it considered bad luck...

592
01:01:45.934 --> 01:01:47.701
to leave the bridal chamber?

593
01:01:50.033 --> 01:01:51.767
It is, my lady.

594
01:01:52.968 --> 01:01:55.400
Once inside the bridal chamber,

595
01:01:56.767 --> 01:01:59.999
the bride and groom must remain there together throughout the night.

596
01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:03.299
They must not leave the room until morning,

597
01:02:03.300 --> 01:02:05.100
or else...

598
01:02:11.234 --> 01:02:13.801
their marriage is believed to be short-lived.

599
01:02:47.234 --> 01:02:49.033
Women do not drink.

600
01:02:49.734 --> 01:02:51.234
It is improper.

601
01:02:51.868 --> 01:02:54.933
I'm not drinking as a woman.

602
01:02:54.934 --> 01:02:57.733
I'm drinking as someone willing to listen.

603
01:02:57.734 --> 01:03:00.600
I won't say a word.

604
01:03:00.601 --> 01:03:03.800
Whatever is on your mind, you can tell me.

605
01:03:03.801 --> 01:03:05.567
I'll listen.

606
01:03:06.267 --> 01:03:08.200
I have nothing to say.

607
01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:13.033
Then... we can drink in silence.

608
01:03:41.934 --> 01:03:43.734
Your older cousin...

609
01:03:46.267 --> 01:03:48.734
cried on her wedding night.

610
01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:54.968
I don't know why.

611
01:03:58.434 --> 01:04:00.667
I only know that she's unhappy.

612
01:04:05.067 --> 01:04:07.934
How can our marriage ever work...

613
01:04:10.467 --> 01:04:12.601
when the man who is supposed to be her life partner...

614
01:04:13.601 --> 01:04:15.968
can't make her happy?

615
01:04:19.734 --> 01:04:21.767
I don't deserve her.

616
01:04:23.801 --> 01:04:26.533
My cousin and you...

617
01:04:26.534 --> 01:04:28.868
are well suited for each other.

618
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.200
But perhaps you just need time.

619
01:04:34.133 --> 01:04:37.701
Once Maneethip gets to know you better,

620
01:04:38.667 --> 01:04:41.267
I'm sure she'll be happy.

621
01:04:43.067 --> 01:04:44.634
You know that.

622
01:04:49.534 --> 01:04:52.000
How can your cousin not see that?

623
01:05:04.767 --> 01:05:06.734
Your words...

624
01:05:07.934 --> 01:05:09.801
bring me comfort.

625
01:05:10.567 --> 01:05:12.701
At least I have you,

626
01:05:13.868 --> 01:05:17.099
who sees something good in me.

627
01:05:17.100 --> 01:05:18.801
Of course I do.

628
01:05:19.701 --> 01:05:23.299
You're calm and gentle.

629
01:05:23.300 --> 01:05:25.900
You can be a little strict at times,

630
01:05:25.901 --> 01:05:27.868
but that's only because you care.

631
01:05:30.601 --> 01:05:34.968
Maneethip is the luckiest woman... to have you as her life partner.

632
01:05:37.100 --> 01:05:42.367
Then I'm lucky... to have spoken with you tonight, too.

633
01:05:44.367 --> 01:05:46.534
Any man who has you as his life partner...

634
01:05:48.767 --> 01:05:51.200
would be the luckiest man alive.

635
01:05:52.801 --> 01:05:54.934
More like the most unfortunate.

636
01:06:42.033 --> 01:06:43.766
Which way is Wat Khao Nam Saeng? [Next Episode]

637
01:06:43.767 --> 01:06:47.366
If you wish to find out, get in the boat and help me pick lotuses.

638
01:06:47.367 --> 01:06:49.200
You'll bruise it if you hold it like that.

639
01:06:52.634 --> 01:06:57.166
I wish to know everything about Maneethip, especially her past.

640
01:06:57.167 --> 01:07:01.833
If Your Majesty would grant me a favor, I have a request to make.

641
01:07:01.834 --> 01:07:02.668
Speak.

642
01:07:02.669 --> 01:07:07.466
The King has issued a royal decree appointing Lady Fongnuan

643
01:07:07.467 --> 01:07:11.166
as an outer court lady-in-waiting at the in Wiang Kaew,

644
01:07:11.167 --> 01:07:12.800
effective immediately.

645
01:07:12.801 --> 01:07:16.032
She may have been meant to serve at the inner court.

646
01:07:16.033 --> 01:07:18.533
Fongnuan was appointed an outer court lady-in-waiting,

647
01:07:18.534 --> 01:07:20.333
not the inner court.

648
01:07:20.334 --> 01:07:21.633
Look into this matter.

649
01:07:21.634 --> 01:07:23.666
It is important to both of us.

650
01:07:23.667 --> 01:07:25.166
I wish to be prepared.

651
01:07:25.167 --> 01:07:27.132
You should accept this royal decree.

652
01:07:27.133 --> 01:07:29.667
Accept the royal decree at once, Fongnuan.
